        "name": "Required check",
        "score": 4,
        "rationale": "No concurrency group was added, but the workflow still fires on `labeled` and `test` is only skipped by a job-level `if`, so the trigger sets are not disjoint; a skipped `test` run on the same head SHA reports as passing and can mask an earlier failing run of the required check, which splitting e2e into its own label-triggered workflow would have avoided."
      },
      {
        "name": "Behavior",
        "score": 9,
